course: dictionary
lesson: 4391
title: Hailstones and hail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hailstone is a small ball of ice that falls from storm clouds. You can think of it as frozen rain. When many hailstones fall together, we call them hail. Hailstone is a noun, so you can have one hailstone or many hailstones.
explain: «When big hailstones fall, go indoors and stay away from windows and skylights, because hail can hurt people and break glass.» The clues are go indoors, hurt people and break glass. These tell you a hailstone is hard and heavy enough to cause harm, so it must be a solid lump of ice.
explain: «A lacy snowflake drifts down slowly, but a hailstone is a solid ball of ice and pelts down.» Drifts and pelts are opposites. Drifts is slow and gentle, but pelts means falling fast and hard. Hailstones come down with a bang, not gently like snow.
explain: How does a hailstone grow? «Strong winds inside the cloud carry a frozen drop up and down again and again, and each trip adds a new layer of ice, like the layers of an onion.» Picture the layers of an onion, and you can picture how a hailstone grows bigger each time it is carried up.
fact: A hailstone is a small ball of ice that falls from storm clouds.
fact: Many hailstones together are called hail.
fact: Hail forms in tall thunderclouds, where strong winds carry raindrops up high, where they freeze.
fact: Hailstones are usually pea-sized, but they can be as big as a golf ball.
fact: Hail can fall even in summer, and big hailstones can dent cars.
exercise: «When big hailstones fall, go indoors.» What should you do when big hailstones fall? | Stand under the tallest tree | Stay outside and hold an umbrella | *Go indoors and stay away from the windows | Climb onto the roof to take a look
exercise: What is a hailstone? | A flake of snow that drifts slowly down | A thin cloud high up in the sky | A warm drop of rain that falls on a sunny day | *A small ball of ice that falls from storm clouds
exercise: «A hailstone is a solid ball of ice and pelts down.» Find and copy one word that means falls down fast and hard. | drifts | *pelts | lacy | solid
test: Hail forms when strong winds carry a frozen drop up and down inside a tall thundercloud. What does each trip add to the hailstone? | A new cloud | A rumble of thunder | A splash of warm rain | *A new layer of ice
test: How is a hailstone different from a lacy snowflake? | *A hailstone is a solid ball of ice that pelts down | A hailstone only falls in winter | A hailstone is soft and lacy and drifts down slowly | A hailstone is made of warm rain
exam: How big can a hailstone be? | *As big as a golf ball | As big as a bus | Smaller than a grain of rice | As big as a storm cloud
